<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ainu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ainu people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ainu are an indigenous people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hokkaido">Hokkaido</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakhalin">Sakhalin</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuril-islands">Kuril Islands</a>, with their own language, religion and culture centred on hunting, fishing and trade. From the 15th century they came under growing pressure from Japanese settlers, and after 1869 Hokkaido was colonised and Ainu customs suppressed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> formally recognised them as an indigenous people in 2008 and 2019.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ainu.jpg" alt="Ainu" width="320" height="326" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Torbenbrinker · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AinuSan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
